<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Francisco de León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1752</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Francisco de León was a Canary Islands-born <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> planter and local official in the Spanish province of Venezuela. In 1749 he led an armed march on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guipuzcoan-company-of-caracas">Guipuzcoan Company of Caracas</a>, whose monopoly hurt local growers, and demanded the expulsion of its Basque agents. After the revolt was suppressed he surrendered, and he died a prisoner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1752.</p></div>
